# Portfolio Snapshot

## Purpose

This is the live summary of current portfolio posture, model allocations, and active review notes.

Use it for recurring review, not hype.

Role in the stack:
- this is the canonical portfolio-posture and model-allocation note
- it owns overall posture, draft weights, cash, and portfolio-level review flags
- it does not own exact deployment triggers or gate-by-gate entry decisions, which belong in [[03. Portfolio/Execution Board]]

## Portfolio posture

- **Date:** 2026-05-20
- **Data as of:** 2026-05-20 technical refresh
- **Macro regime:** restrictive pause, resilient growth baseline, selective risk-on
- **Overall posture:** selective risk-on with reduced confidence
- **Cash level:** 10% target cash after the 2026-05-07 owner posture decision
- **Drawdown from recent high:** not applicable; still model-draft stage
- **Capital base assumption:** **$10,000 flat** approved by Randall on 2026-05-18 for real-capital-quality deployment planning and paper-trading preparation
- **Sizing note:** keep draft weights subordinate to the written risk framework. A fresh in-band signal still does not overrule concentration limits, crowding risk, or warning-grade trust. For the current $10k capital base, default implementation planning assumes fractional-share availability plus two-tranche sizing; whole-share-only execution is acceptable only when it stays inside intended tier and concentration rules.
- **Capital-base implementation overlay:** with 10% cash retained, investable capital is **$9,000**. Practical starter zones are **$400-$600** for Tier 1 names, **$200-$350** for Tier 2 names, and **$50-$150** for Tier 3/speculative names. GS remains impractical for intended Tier 2 sizing as a one-share whole-share order; use fractions or defer/re-tier explicitly. LMT remains blocked regardless of share math.
- **Current priority order:** ETN remains the first real-capital-quality deployment and paper-readiness candidate, subject to fresh quote/band/stop checks and WF67 guardrails. ETFs stay eligible in the active deployment universe when they solve portfolio-construction problems better than single names: VXUS for international diversification and ITA for conditional Defense/aerospace exposure remain review candidates, not automatic buys. GOOG / MSFT / GS remain real-capital candidates but are not deployable now because of no-chase, Tech-cap, Financials sequencing, or sizing constraints. JPM, LMT, RTX, BKNG, BRK.B, LNG, and XOM remain repair/blocked/bench until reclaim or fresh review. Detail lives in the Execution Board, not this snapshot.

