- This is still a model draft, not an execution-ready account snapshot.
- Draft weights are not live allocations and do not grant trade authority.
- LIN is now a formal Materials sleeve/starter-sizing planning candidate at 0% active / 3% conditional planning weight / $200-$350 starter context, but remains non-deployed and non-executable until fresh quote/band confirmation plus separate order authority.
- ETN remains the first Tier 1 explicit-add priority and remains manual-only.
- MSFT is owner-promoted as a staged manual candidate, but current state is above-band / no-chase and below the 200-day; no fresh sizing action until pullback or explicit approved band review plus Tech-cap sequencing.
- JPM approval remains recorded, but the current trigger is not live: latest evidence has it below the formal trigger band and below the 301.17 stop. Treat JPM as do-not-touch / below-stop until band reclaim or explicit band review clears the setup.
- GOOG, GS, and NVDA require better entry quality or event resolution before any deployment escalation.
- BKNG is near-stop repair/no-chase; BRK.B, LMT, watch-lane LNG, and RTX are below-stop or repair-state names. Do not soften any of these into deployment entitlement without a fresh reclaim/review.
- Direct Tech is already at the written cap; MSFT deployment requires an explicit sequencing decision and fresh price/band confirmation before any real sizing action. Audit-remediation packet: `tmp/audit-remediation-portfolio-decision-packets.md`.
- Defense gap accounting is now explicit: LMT is **0% active / prior 10% suspended**, KTOS is the only active Defense exposure at **2% speculative**, RTX remains 0% watch/repair, and ITA remains **0% active** with a conditional future **5% / $500** planning cap only after look-through acceptance and gates. No paper/live order, brokerage/account action, money movement, cash change, or execution authority is granted.
- Active-deployment universe rule: for the $10k account, ETFs are valid candidates when they improve diversification, reduce single-name sizing distortion, or express a desired sleeve more cleanly than blocked/high-price single names. ETF eligibility still requires written model/sleeve/sizing acceptance and WF67 guardrails before any paper execution.
- If total model drawdown exceeds 6% to 8%, force a full review.

## Freshness and refresh policy

- **Last updated:** 2026-05-19 - Randall promoted LIN into a formal Materials sleeve / starter-sizing planning lane at 0% active / 3% conditional planning weight / $200-$350 starter context. This is workspace model/sleeve planning only: no live trade, paper order, brokerage/account action, money movement, owner-approval inference, or external execution entitlement.
- **Data as of:** 2026-05-19 technical refresh for current Execution Board/deployment surfaces; other technical rows remain governed by the Execution Board freshness fields
- **Refresh cadence:** after Execution Board refreshes, tracked earnings, material macro regime changes, or any draft sizing decision
- **Next refresh due:** when a model weight, sleeve role, concentration limit, or portfolio-level status changes materially
- **Refresh policy:** update posture, weights, risk flags, and status lines when the Execution Board, macro regime, or catalyst map changes materially. Do not treat draft weights as live allocations.

## Recommended review actions

1. Use [[03. Portfolio/Execution Board]] for live decision state.
2. Use [[03. Portfolio/Execution Board]] for exact bands, stops, repair zones, and invalidation.
3. Use [[04. Research/Coverage and Watchlist]] for thesis, key risk, and act-when conditions.
4. Review the audit-remediation owner-decision packets in `tmp/audit-remediation-portfolio-decision-packets.md`:
   - MSFT: prefer 40/60 planning weight, no Tech-cap exception, no action until fresh band confirmation.
   - LMT / Defense: implemented as model-accounting maintenance on 2026-05-18: LMT 0% active / prior 10% suspended, KTOS 2% speculative placeholder, RTX 0%, ITA 0% active with conditional 5% future planning cap after look-through acceptance and gates.
5. Use the $10k flat capital framework for all new deployment and paper-trading preparation: $1,000 cash reserve, $9,000 investable, fractional shares + two-tranche sizing by default; do not force GS or other high-price names into oversized whole-share allocations.
6. Build paper-trading candidates from the **real-capital eligible universe**, not from convenience-only mechanics. ETN is first; ETFs such as VXUS/ITA can be eligible only after their model/sleeve/sizing gates clear.
7. Revisit draft weights only when blocker status, setup quality, thesis conviction, or concentration posture actually changes and WF64/WF56 gated validators support the apply.
8. Keep watch-only and repair-mode names explicitly benched until new evidence changes their lane.
